## Task

Apply fixes for each finding. Re-run tests through the same
skill-driven path verify-tests uses (i.e. through the skill's test
shim when available, otherwise the fallback command). Set
`verdict = approved` ONLY when:

1. Tests pass locally under the same test command verify-tests
   would resolve, AND
2. All findings are cleared.

Otherwise set `verdict = revise`. The loop latch reads `verdict`
to decide whether to re-run review-diffs.

Commit to the chosen fix approach across iterations; revisit only
when a subsequent review finding directly contradicts it.

## Output

```bash
